  "schema_version": "2.0",
  "report_markdown": "## Executive Summary\n\n- Hema Malini is the sitting MP of the Mathura constituency in Uttar Pradesh, currently serving her third consecutive term since 2014.\n- The city of Mathura lies within the cultural region of Braj.\n- According to the 2011 census on Mathura NPP, 95.4% of the people identified as Hindi speakers.\n- The city gets its name from Mahishasura or Mahishuru.\n- The city is named after the presiding deity at Mangaladevi Temple.\n- Indore is the largest city of the Indian state of Madhya Pradesh.\n- Indore has an estimated population of 5.6 million in 2025.\n- Between 1951 and 2011, Muslims grew by 4.4 percentage points to 14.2% of the population, while Hindus declined by 4.3 points to 79.8%.\n- Raja Ravi Varma was born into an aristocratic family of Kerala.\n- Raja Ravi Varma was best known for his lush portraits of beautiful women from wealthy homes, goddesses of the Hindu pantheon and mythological characters.\n- Temple, Texas grew from 82,652 residents in 2020 to 93,095 people counted in 2023.\n- Temple is the fastest growing city in central Texas.\n- Temple's population hit 102,000 residents.\n- Temple is one of seven cities in Texas noted as the fastest growing U.S. cities, and six of those are between the Metroplex (Dallas-Fort Worth) and San Antonio up and down Interstate 35, including Temple.\n- Raja Ravi Varma was born on April 29, 1848, at Kilimanoor Palace, near Trivandrum, Travancore princely state, British India [now Thiruvananthapuram, Kerala, India].\n- Raja Ravi Varma died on October 2, 1906, at Kilimanoor Palace.\n",
